tasks.description:
Under `# Task 4`, write a function called `report` that takes a list of `(hill, callouts, hours)` tuples and gives back a list of the lines of the table, as texts:

1. a heading line: `Hill` on the left of 14 characters, `Calls` on the right of 6 and `Hours` on the right of 8;
2. one row for each tuple, in order, made as `report_row` makes it;
3. a total line, made as `report_row` makes it, with `Total` as the hill, the callouts added up and the hours added up.

For an empty list it gives back the heading and a total line of zeros. Print each line of what it gives back for `by_hill`.

Check calls `report` with lists of its own and looks at the lines it gives back. It gives your file its own `report_row` first, so a mistake in Task 3 does not count here.
